{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791296249,"nonce":"BTMKhBeDQZGRPLdLHveEqDb9/N8=","title":"Float values pushed through Array\u003cAny\u003e are read as integer bits by an Int array","message":"At 95149065f23ef8f0202ac6c694dc243cea0b3984, Issue10124 test2 calls an extension taking arr:Array\u003cAny\u003e and ...values:Float with an Array\u003cInt\u003e receiver. Packed rest arguments and Float iterator reads are now correct, but arr.push(v) stores raw Float bits in the receiver, which remains statically read as Int. Assert.same([1,3,4,5,6,7], arr) sees [1,3,4,4617315517961601024,4618441417868443648,4619567317775286272].\n\nHaxe accepts this and compares numeric values across the erased Array\u003cAny\u003e boundary. The current raw-slot array representation has no per-slot scalar tag to recover that distinction. A fix must maintain shared array mutation semantics rather than silently passing a copy into the extension.\n\nFull default tiered report /tmp/rayzor-rest-extension-final/report.tsv scores Issue10124 WRONG_ANSWER. Test1 and test3 pass in /tmp/rayzor-rest-extension-isolated.log (CONFORMANCE_OK 3). The extension-packing issue 5ef3f95fa58061da6bf8ad24b2064c51388656d900215b4b26296af61b4c440d is closed separately.","files":null}]}